description: |
  Retrieves the list of Cortex tenant console users (operators, analysts, administrators who log into the Cortex platform itself) along with their core properties (email, first/last name, role, last login, type, groups, scope), optionally filtered by email addresses and/or names. Use this action to resolve a Cortex console user from a display name or partial identifier to a canonical "user_email" before passing them to another action (for example, setting a case assignee or adding a case team member). Do NOT use this action to enrich an investigation subject (an employee or identity observed in alerts/events) or to look up risk levels, directory attributes, or data from external identity providers - this action only returns Cortex platform accounts. Disambiguation rules - when the user is identified by name (the "names" argument):
    - If exactly one user matches, use their "user_email".
    - If multiple users match, do NOT guess - ask the requester which user they meant.
    - If zero users match, do NOT substitute the raw name string for a real email - inform the requester and ask for a more specific name or an email address.
  Note: The default result size is 50 users; the data returned may be partial.
